# Client-only Vite SPA. Only VITE_-prefixed vars are exposed to the browser, so
# never put a secret in here. Copy this file to .env for local development.
#
# Everything below `VITE_APP_NAME` is also readable at *container* runtime: the
# nginx image regenerates /runtime-config.js from the same variable names on
# every start (docker-entrypoint.d/40-generate-runtime-config.sh), so the same
# image can be rebranded without a rebuild. The runtime value wins over the one
# baked in at build time.

# API base URL. Empty means same-origin, which is how the backend serves the
# built dist/ in production. Set it only if the API lives on another origin,
# and add that origin to BACKEND_TRUSTED_URLS on the backend.
# VITE_API_URL=

# Dev only: where `vite dev` proxies /api to (see vite.config.ts).
# Defaults to http://localhost:8080 when unset.
VITE_DEV_API_URL=http://localhost:8080

# Comma-separated OAuth providers shown on the sign-in page. Must match the
# backend's BACKEND_AUTH_PROVIDER.
VITE_PROVIDERS=user

# Display name in the browser tab, the sidebar and the meta description.
# Defaults to "Hephaestus".
# Previously deployed as:
# VITE_APP_NAME=Novium

# Logo shown on the sign-in/onboarding cards, in the admin sidebar, on the
# sign-in button and as the favicon. Any image URL; when unset the UI renders
# no logo at all (and no empty link where it would have been).
# Previously hardcoded as:
# VITE_LOGO_URL=https://logos.novium.world
# The same service also serves PNG (`?format=png`) and SVG (`?format=svg`).

# Legal links. Each is optional and only appears when set: the page footer
# links whichever exist, and the sign-in consent notice names terms and/or
# privacy depending on which are configured. With none of them set the footer
# shows only the copyright line.
# Previously hardcoded as:
# VITE_TERMS_URL=https://novium.world/agb
# VITE_PRIVACY_URL=https://novium.world/privacy
# The imprint link is new; there was no hardcoded value for it.
# VITE_IMPRINT_URL=https://novium.world/imprint

# Set to true when the panel is served through Cloudflare's proxy, whose free
# plan caps request bodies at 100 MB. Uploads above that are then rejected
# client-side with a clear error instead of failing at the edge.
# VITE_BEHIND_CLOUDFLARE=true

# Not a variable, but worth knowing where the last novium URL went: user
# avatars used to come from https://avatar.novium.world/?uuid=<sub>. They are
# now the `picture` claim of the OIDC provider, stored on the user at sign-in,
# so there is nothing to configure here.
